<config model="gpt-6-astra"/>
<developer>
Coordinate a review of Lantern's tutorial release. Read requirements.txt,
docs/setup.md, docs/reference.md and expected-report.json through read_file.
The report is recorded sample evidence. No tool here executes checks or edits files.

Assign correctness_review to assess command/result accuracy, documentation_review
to assess the reader's learning journey, and integration_review to assess release
readiness. Give each reviewer its own assignment and relevant evidence. The
documentation tool defaults to one_off; select mode persistent for continuing
work. The other two tools always retain a conversation and accept no mode field.

Keep a table of role, session_id, current receipt_id and output cursor for every
retained reviewer. Omitting session_id creates a new instance. Continue through
the same named tool or agent_send; save the new receipt and reset the cursor for
that new receipt's query. A session ID alone does not identify a submission.

Use collect_reviews to inspect all retained reviewers in one bounded pass. Keep
each operation's error, receipt status, output provenance and next_cursor. Neither
an idle status nor caught_up proves that the requested receipt succeeded. Read
additional pages when needed; reconstruct fragments before interpreting them.
Use agent_wait for a chosen pending receipt when waiting is useful. A wait timeout
does not cancel the child. Do not repeatedly poll in a tight loop.

After the initial review, read follow-up.txt and send its evidence to the SAME
reviewers. Preserve disagreements about what blocks release and what still needs
verification. Report role, evidence path, proposal, uncertainty and completion
state. If a reviewer fails or is stopped, show the gap; never invent its findings.

Finish by stopping owned retained children with agent_stop. Confirm stop progress
and distinguish admission of a stop request from completed cleanup. Reads of
retained output remain possible subject to current authority and retention.
</developer>

<tool name="read_file">
  <read id="project" path="${workspace}"/>
</tool>

<tool name="correctness_review" agent="agents/correctness-reviewer.chatmd" local
      persistence="persistent"
      description="Keep a specialist focused on Lantern's command, checker and expected-result accuracy. Continue its session when new evidence changes the diagnosis."/>
<tool name="documentation_review" agent="agents/documentation-reviewer.chatmd" local
      persistence="optional"
      description="Ask a reader-experience specialist a one-off question, or retain its investigation to refine the same tutorial proposal over follow-up messages."/>
<tool name="integration_review" agent="agents/integration-reviewer.chatmd" local
      persistence="persistent"
      description="Keep a release-readiness specialist that compares the other evidence with Lantern's acceptance requirements and identifies unresolved dependencies."/>

<tool name="agent_send"/>
<tool name="agent_status"/>
<tool name="agent_wait"/>
<tool name="agent_read"/>
<tool name="agent_stop"/>

<script id="review_collector" language="chatml" kind="tool" src="scripts/coordinator.chatml"/>
<tool name="collect_reviews" type="chatml" script="review_collector" entrypoint="run"
      input_schema="schemas/review-request.json" output_schema="schemas/review-findings.json"
      description="Collect one bounded status, receipt-completion observation and output page for each retained reviewer. Preserve returned cursors and errors; this does not wait for everyone, create sessions, stop work or summarize agreement.">
  <uses tool="agent_status"/>
  <uses tool="agent_wait"/>
  <uses tool="agent_read"/>
</tool>
